import Foundation

enum FavoritesLibrary {
    static let items: [FavoriteItem] = [
        FavoriteItem(title: "The Kiss", subtitle: " Gustav Klimt · 1907 – 1908", imageName: "image1", rating: 5, details: "The Kiss shows a couple embracing, wrapped in robes covered with gold patterns. Klimt painted it at the peak of his Golden Period, when he often used real gold leaf. The painting is kept in the Belvedere museum in Vienna. Its flat, ornamental style makes the two figures look like one glowing shape."
                    ),
        FavoriteItem(title: "Impression, Sunrise", subtitle: "Claude Monet · 1872", imageName: "image2", rating: 4, details: "Impression, Sunrise captures the port of Le Havre at dawn under a cool, misty sky with a bright orange sun breaking through. Small dark boats glide across the water while loose brushstrokes form shimmering reflections. Monet painted it quickly from life, giving the Impressionist movement its name. It is kept at the Musée Marmottan Monet in Paris."),
        FavoriteItem(title: "Turksib", subtitle: "Abilkhan Kasteev · 1969", imageName: "image3", rating: 5, details: "Turksib depicts the arrival of the first train during the construction of the Turkestan–Siberia railway across the Kazakh steppe. Local riders and residents in traditional clothing watch the locomotive against wide hills and an open sky. Kasteev celebrated modernization and changing life in Kazakhstan through warm, narrative colors. The painting is part of the Kasteev State Museum of Arts in Almaty."),
        FavoriteItem(title: "Ophelia", subtitle: "John Everett Millais · 1851 – 1852", imageName: "image4", rating: 4, details: "Ophelia shows Shakespeare's tragic character floating in a forest stream surrounded by wildflowers and a willow tree. Millais painted the riverbanks and plants outdoors with fine botanical detail and symbolic meaning. The model Elizabeth Siddal posed in a bathtub kept warm by lamps beneath it. The work is housed in Tate Britain in London."),
        FavoriteItem(title: "Almond Blossoms", subtitle: "Vincent van Gogh · 1890", imageName: "image5", rating: 4, details: "Almond Blossoms features delicate white and pale pink blossoms against a bright turquoise-blue spring sky. Van Gogh painted it to celebrate the birth of his nephew, making the blooming branches a symbol of new life. Influenced by Japanese woodblock prints, the composition has clear outlines and calm balance. It is kept at the Van Gogh Museum in Amsterdam."),
        FavoriteItem(title: "Hunters in the Snow", subtitle: "Pieter Bruegel the Elder · 1565", imageName: "image6", rating: 4, details: "Hunters in the Snow shows tired hunters with dogs returning to a snow-covered village as others skate on frozen ponds below. Steep, craggy mountains rise in the distance under a pale winter sky. Bruegel created it as part of a seasonal cycle that captures everyday life in harmony with nature. The painting is held at the Kunsthistorisches Museum in Vienna."),
        FavoriteItem(title: "The Black Sea ", subtitle: "Ivan Aivazovsky · 1881", imageName: "image7", rating: 5, details: "The Black Sea presents a vast expanse of dark, rolling waves beneath heavy storm clouds and a distant sail. Aivazovsky painted mostly from memory and imagination, focusing on light, transparency, and the movement of water. The quiet horizon and deep tones give the scene a sense of scale and solitude. It is kept in the State Russian Museum in St. Petersburg."),
        FavoriteItem(title: "Spring", subtitle: "Aisha Galimbaeva · 1972", imageName: "image8", rating: 5, details: "Spring portrays Kazakh women in festive national attire gathered in a blooming orchard with mountains in the background. One woman plays the dombra while white and soft pink blossoms echo the lightness of their garments. Galimbaeva, the first professional Kazakh woman painter, brought lyrical warmth and musicality to her scenes. The painting is in the Almaty Museum of Arts collection."),
        FavoriteItem(title: "Portrait of Shara Zhienkulova", subtitle: "Gulfairus Ismailova · 1958", imageName: "image9", rating: 5, details: "Portrait of Shara Zhienkulova captures the celebrated Kazakh dancer mid-movement in an ornate crimson-and-gold stage costume. Ismailova worked closely with theater and dance, giving the figure poise, rhythm, and expressive energy. Rich warm tones highlight the grace of her posture and traditional ornament. The work belongs to the Kasteev State Museum of Arts in Almaty."),
        FavoriteItem(title: "Water Lilies", subtitle: "Claude Monet · 1906", imageName: "image10", rating: 3, details: "Water Lilies focuses on floating lily pads, blossoms, and sky reflections across the pond in Monet's garden at Giverny. By omitting the horizon line, Monet turned the water's surface into an immersive field of color and light. Soft touches of blue, green, and rose evoke quiet contemplation. Examples from this series are held in major collections including the Musée de l'Orangerie in Paris." ),
        FavoriteItem(title: "Rainbow", subtitle: "Ivan Aivazovsky · 1873", imageName: "image11", rating: 5, details: "Rainbow shows a glowing arc of light breaking through stormy mist above turbulent waves and a struggling boat. Sailors work to guide their vessel while bright light illuminates the wet spray and dark sea. Aivazovsky contrasted dramatic danger with a hopeful burst of color in the sky. The painting is kept in the State Russian Museum in St. Petersburg."),
        FavoriteItem(title: "The Wounded Angel", subtitle: "Hugo Simberg · 1903", imageName: "image12", rating: 2, details: "The Wounded Angel depicts two somber boys carrying a blindfolded angel with a stained wing on a stretcher through a quiet landscape. Simberg left the meaning open, inviting viewers to read their own thoughts into the mysterious procession. Calm Nordic scenery contrasts with the emotional weight of the figures. It is held in the Ateneum Art Museum in Helsinki."),
        FavoriteItem(title: "Woman with a Parasol", subtitle: "Claude Monet · 1875", imageName: "image13", rating: 5, details: "Woman with a Parasol shows Monet's wife Camille holding a green parasol on a breezy hillside with their young son nearby. Wind catches her white dress and veil while bright sunlight filters through tall grass and clouds. Painted outdoors with lively brushwork, it captures a fleeting moment of summer air and motion. The painting is kept at the National Gallery of Art in Washington, D.C."),
        FavoriteItem(title: "A Sunday Afternoon on the Island of La Grande Jatte", subtitle: "Georges Seurat · 1884 – 1886", imageName: "image14", rating: 3, details: "A Sunday Afternoon on the Island of La Grande Jatte depicts Parisians relaxing, strolling, and boating along the Seine on a sunny afternoon. Seurat built the scene from tiny dots of pure color using divisionism, creating luminous harmony from afar. Structured poses give the lively crowd a calm, almost timeless stillness. It is housed at the Art Institute of Chicago."),
        FavoriteItem(title: "Among the Waves", subtitle: "Ivan Aivazovsky · 1898", imageName: "image15", rating: 5, details: "Among the Waves fills the canvas with towering, translucent sea swells and white foam with no shore or ships in sight. Warm sunlight filters through the crest of the largest wave, illuminating its emerald depth. Aivazovsky painted the canvas late in life with bold, sweeping energy. It is kept at the Aivazovsky National Art Gallery in Feodosia."),
        FavoriteItem(title: "Dance at Le Moulin de la Galette", subtitle: "Pierre-Auguste Renoir · 1876", imageName: "image16", rating: 3, details: "Dance at Le Moulin de la Galette captures a lively weekend gathering in an open-air dance garden on Montmartre. Dappled sunlight passes through the trees onto couples dancing, chatting, and enjoying the afternoon. Renoir used soft, warm strokes to convey sociability and joyful movement. The painting is held at the Musée d'Orsay in Paris."),
        FavoriteItem(title: "Kok-par", subtitle: "Kanafia Telzhanov · 1960", imageName: "image17", rating: 5, details: "Kok-par depicts riders charging across the steppe in a fast, physical contest of the traditional Kazakh equestrian game. Dust rises around galloping horses as players compete for control under a broad sky. Telzhanov used dynamic brushwork and bold composition to convey speed and steppe spirit. The work is in the collection of the Kasteev State Museum of Arts in Almaty."),
        FavoriteItem(title: "Wanderer above the Sea of Fog", subtitle: "Caspar David Friedrich · c. 1818", imageName: "image18", rating: 3, details: "Wanderer above the Sea of Fog shows a traveler standing with his back to the viewer on a rocky peak above dense mist. Mountain ridges emerge faintly through the fog beneath pale, shifting clouds. The central figure reflects Romantic themes of solitude, awe, and contemplation before nature. It is kept at the Hamburger Kunsthalle in Hamburg."),
        FavoriteItem(title: "The Garden of Earthly Delights", subtitle: "Hieronymus Bosch · c. 1490–1510", imageName: "image19", rating: 3, details: "The Garden of Earthly Delights is a large triptych filled with imaginative figures, oversized fruit, strange creatures, and symbolic scenes. Its three panels move from Edenic beginnings to a crowded world of earthly pleasures and a dark hellscape. Bosch packed the composition with intricate details that reward close inspection over time. The painting is kept at the Museo del Prado in Madrid."),
        FavoriteItem(title: "Girl with a Pearl Earring", subtitle: "Johannes Vermeer · c. 1665", imageName: "image20", rating: 5, details: "Girl with a Pearl Earring shows a young woman turning her head toward the viewer with parted lips and a bright gaze. She wears a blue-and-gold headscarf and a large pearl earring that catches a crisp highlight. Vermeer used soft light and a dark background to make her expression feel immediate and lifelike. The painting is housed in the Mauritshuis in The Hague.")
    ]
}
